---
import HubPage from '../components/HubPage.astro';
---
<HubPage hubId="investing">
  <section aria-labelledby="hub-guide" class="mt-12 max-w-3xl">
    <h2 id="hub-guide" class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-4">How to choose an investment calculator</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Start with how the money goes in. For a fixed monthly amount into a mutual fund, use the <a href="/sip-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">SIP calculator</a>; for a single deposit left to grow, use <a href="/lump-sum-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">lump sum</a> or <a href="/compound-interest-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">compound interest</a>. Simple interest only applies when interest is paid out rather than reinvested.</p>
    <p data-currency-lock="INR" class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">For bank deposits, the <a href="/fd-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">FD calculator</a> handles one deposit and the <a href="/rd-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">RD calculator</a> handles fixed monthly deposits. Indian savers after tax-free long-term returns should check the <a href="/in/ppf-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">PPF calculator</a>; US savers should use the <a href="/us/401k-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">401(k) calculator</a>.</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">To judge returns you have already earned, use <a href="/cagr-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">CAGR</a> when there is one start value and one end value, and <a href="/xirr-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">XIRR</a> when you added or withdrew money on different dates. Then run any target through the <a href="/inflation-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">inflation calculator</a> and let the <a href="/savings-goal-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">savings goal calculator</a> turn it into a monthly amount.</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">To compare interest-crediting schedules on one deposit, use the <a href="/compound-interest-calculator" class="text-accent font-medium hover:underline">compound interest calculator for daily, monthly and annual growth</a>. Keep the same nominal rate and term while changing the frequency.</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">For one-off sums such as simple interest, present value or the effect of inflation on a price, the <a href="/everyday-math" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">everyday money math hub</a> groups the basic formulas in one place.</p>
  </section>
</HubPage>
